    },
    "body": "It happens when you come to bogus comment state from `markup declaration open` state. If `!` in that state is not followed by doctype, comment hypnes or CDATA (if it's enabled by parser) then any character after it should be reconsumed in `bogus comment` state. It's not quite obvious from the spec, since  `markup declaration open` state is not formalized as well:\n\n> Switch to the bogus comment state. The next character that is consumed, if any, is the first character that will be in the comment.\n\nState description doesn't have \"Consume the next input character\" prefix. Therefore no character is consumed since the last state. Speaking clearly we just use lookahead here.\n",
    "created_at": "2016-04-05T21:47:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-06T10:09:31Z",
